    description: 'Owner complaint: "he answer is weired and no comprensible: <dispatch_subagent id=\\"quill\\" task=\\"...\\" />" — the agent was leaking raw XML tags as the final answer.\n\nROOT CAUSES (4 bugs found):\n\n1. DISPATCH_SUBAGENT_RE regex only handled PAIRED tags `<dispatch_subagent id=\\"x\\">task</dispatch_subagent>`.\n   It did NOT match self-closing format `<dispatch_subagent id=\\"x\\" task=\\"...\\"/>` (which the LLM often emits).\n   Result: parsed.dispatch was undefined → fell through to "final answer path" → raw XML leaked as the answer.\n\n2. finalAnswer cleanup only stripped `<dispatch agent=...>` (DISPATCH_RE) but NOT `<dispatch_subagent ...>`.\n   So even when dispatch was correctly parsed, any leftover self-closing tag text leaked to the user.\n\n3. LLM invented pseudo-XML tags: `<parallel_executor>{json}</parallel_executor>`, `<reasoning_trace>`, `<execution>`, `<plan>`, `<action>`, `<reflect>`.\n   None of these are real tools — the correct syntax is `<tool name=\\"parallel_executor\\">{json}</tool>`.\n   Pseudo-XML leaked as raw text.\n\n4. No dispatch cap → agent dispatched 6+ subagents in a chain (Quill → Forge → Aurora → Scout → Pulse → Echo) without synthesizing, then hit MAX_ITERATIONS and produced a useless "I\'ve reached my iteration limit" fallback.\n\nFIXES APPLIED:\n\n1. New DISPATCH_SUBAGENT_RE regex handles ALL 4 formats:\n   (a) <dispatch_subagent id=\\"x\\">task</dispatch_subagent>   (paired)\n   (b) <dispatch_subagent id=\\"x\\" task=\\"...\\"/>                (self-closing w/ task attr)\n   (c) <dispatch_subagent id=\\"x\\"/>                              (self-closing, task in body)\n   (d) <dispatch_subagent id=\\"x\\" task=\\"...\\">task</dispatch_subagent> (mixed)\n\n2. finalAnswer now strips: THOUGHT_RE + DISPATCH_RE + DISPATCH_SUBAGENT_RE + PSEUDO_XML_RE + REASONING_TRACE_BLOCK_RE + safety-net regex for any leftover tags.\n\n3. Added "empty finalAnswer retry" — if cleanup leaves <10 chars, the orchestrator prompts the LLM to give a real answer instead of showing blank.\n\n4. Added DISPATCH CAP: after 3 dispatches in one turn, the orchestrator injects a [SYSTEM] message forcing synthesis. The agent MUST give a final answer at that point.\n\n5. Improved fallback auto-synthesis: now collects BOTH tool results AND [SUBAGENT_RESULT] messages from the conversation (previously only tool results). So if the agent dispatches 3 subagents and hits the cap, the fallback produces a real consolidated summary with all 3 subagent outputs.\n\n6. Updated SYSTEM_PROMPT (agent.ts) and ORCHESTRATOR_PROMPT_ADDENDUM (orchestrator.ts) with:\n   - Strict OUTPUT FORMAT rules listing the FORBIDDEN pseudo-XML tags\n   - Explicit dispatch format examples (both valid forms)\n   - "DISPATCH CAP: Maximum 3 sub-agent dispatches per turn" rule\n   - "Final answer = PLAIN MARKDOWN only" rule\n\nRESULT: The owner will now see clean, structured markdown answers like:\n```\n## Summary\nI dispatched 3 sub-agents to research your e-book passive income plan...\n\n### 🤖 Quill — Trending Topics\nPersonal finance for beginners is the top trending niche with 47k monthly searches...\n\n### 🤖 Forge — E-book Draft\n10,000-word draft outline ready, covering budgeting, saving, debt payoff...\n\n### 🤖 Aurora — Blog + Affiliate\n5 SEO-optimized blog post titles + Amazon Associates + ShareASale signup links...\n\n## Recommendations\n1. Publish e-book on Amazon KDP (free)\n2. Set up blog on Medium (free)\n3. Join Amazon Associates (free)\n\n## Income Projection\n- Month 1: $200-500 (slow start, building audience)\n- Month 3: $1,500-3,000 (organic traffic + email list)\n- Month 6: $5,000-8,000 (compounding affiliate revenue)\n```',
